== Problem

The problem is the same as in the previous lab: select 50% of the nodes to form a Hamiltonian cycle, minimizing sum of edge and node costs.

== 2-regret heuristics

2-regret heuristics are similar to greedy heuristics, but on every iteration, for every node, they compute 2 best placements instead of only the best one. Then, the score used for selecting best placement takes into account _regret_ (how much would we "regret" choosing the 2nd best placement over the best placement). Regret is to be maximized.

The task asks to implement two versions of regret:
- Greedy 2-regret heuristics.
- Greedy heuristics with a weighted sum criterion – 2-regret (`regret`) + best change of the objective function (`delta`)

It can be seen that the weighted version is actually a generalization of both the "plain" greedy 2-regret heuristics (set `delta=0`) and the base non-regret algorithm (set `regret=0`). Therefore, we provide a single pseudocode for both variants.

#import "@preview/lovelace:0.3.0": *


#pseudocode-list(booktabs: true, title: [Weighted greedy 2-regret TSP])[
  + $"tour" := "list"["start_node"]$
  + Append best second node to the `tour` (see find best second node)
  + *while* $|"tour"| < "target_count"$:
    + $"candidates := list[]"$
    + *for* every $"node"$ not yet in the tour:
      + Compute possible placement positions and deltas, depending on the base method (see below)
      + $"best" := "two placements with the lowest delta"$
      + $"regret" := "best"[1]."delta" - "best"[0]."delta"$
      + $"score" := "regret_weight" * "regret" - "delta_weight" * "best"[0]."delta"$
      + Append a tuple $("score", "node", "place")$ to $"candidates"$
    + $"chosen" := "max"_"score" ("candidates")$.
    + Insert $"chosen"."node"$ to the tour at the position $"chosen"."place"$
]

#pseudocode-list(booktabs: true, title: [Find best second node])[
  + Set $w$ to 1 for nearest-neighbor variant or to 2 for greedy-cycle variant.
  + Return $"argmin"("nodes", D[s,n] * w + C[n])$
]

#pseudocode-list(booktabs: true, title: [Placement candidates for nearest-neighbor])[
  + *for* every place where it could be put: before the first node, after the last node, or between two neighbors in the path *do*
    + *if* it goes before the first node *then*
      + price = _distance from it to the first node_ + _its own cost_
    + *else if* it goes after the last node *then*
      + price = _distance from the last node to it_ + _its own cost_
    + *else*
      + price = _distance from the left neighbor to it_ + _distance from it to the right neighbor_ - _the old distance between the two neighbors_ + _its own cost_
    + yield (place, price)
]

#pseudocode-list(booktabs: true, title: [Placement candidates for greedy cycle])[
  + *for* every connection between two neighbors in the tour *do*
    + price := _distance from the left neighbor to the node_ + _distance from the node to the right neighbor_ - _the old distance between the two neighbors_ + _its own cost_
    + yield (place: connection + 1, price)
]

