== Conclusions

If properly weighted, 2-regret is the best algorithm from all the tested ones on average - by roughly 7.8% compared to no-regret version.

However, the plain regret version (delta_weight=0) seems to be much worse than other 2-regrets or even no-regret versions. The difference is smaller for TSPB than for TSPA. Looking at the plots it looks like the algorithm doesn't seem to account for node costs that much anymore. Apart from the delta_weight=0 case, there are no large, consistent differences between weights. Solutions seem to be similar, especially for the greedy cycle variant. Greedy cycle variant seems to be slighly better for TSPA; for TSPB the difference depends on weights. Additionally, nearest-neighbor-anywhere seems to like lon

All best solutions were verified with the solution checker, and the objective values matched.

